// The one process here with no terraform behind it.
//
// Four metres, four sentences and something under two minutes, modelled
// because it happens most days and because nothing in it leaves a trace.
// There is no ticket, no message and no calendar entry at any point. The only
// record the task ever has is two people holding it in their heads, and that
// record has a retention policy nobody chose.
//
// The desks are modelled for one reason: this process is physical. A person
// stands up, crosses a room and comes back, and the two legs of that are the
// only part of the whole exchange that reliably completes. Without a box to
// walk to, both legs collapse into arrows between the same two people and the
// diagram loses the thing it is about.
model {

  office = workplace 'The Office' {
    description '
      One room, two desks four metres apart, and no system of record between
      them. Everything below happens inside it, which is also the reason
      nothing below can be looked up afterwards.
    '

    // =====================================================================
    // The two parties
    // =====================================================================

    t25 = actor 'Theodor 2.5' {
      description '
        The party with the idea, and the only party that moves. Being the one
        who walks is what makes the proposal happen at all: there is no queue
        to put it on, so the task is delivered by carrying it.

        Holds the task in working memory and nowhere else, before, during and
        briefly after.
      '
    }

    t37 = actor 'Theodor 3.7' {
      description '
        The party being asked. Newer, faster, and already committed to
        something at the moment of asking.

        The decline is about capacity and not about the task. Nothing in this
        process ever establishes what the task was worth, because the only
        question put to it is whether there is room for it right now.
      '
    }

    // =====================================================================
    // The furniture
    // =====================================================================

    deskA = workstation 'Desk A' {
      technology 'Four metres from Desk B'
      description 'Where 2.5 starts, and where 2.5 ends up. The two are the same place.'
    }

    deskB = workstation 'Desk B' {
      technology 'Headphones, usually on'
      description '
        Where 3.7 is. Also the only address the proposal has: it cannot be
        sent here, so it has to be brought.
      '
    }

    // =====================================================================
    // The task, and what becomes of it
    // =====================================================================

    task = work-item 'The Proposed Task' {
      technology 'Spoken, once'
      description '
        Whatever it was. The model deliberately does not say, because by the
        end of the sequence neither party can either.

        It exists in exactly two copies for the length of one conversation,
        both of them in heads, and it is never serialised into anything that
        outlives the walk back.
      '
    }

    nowhere = oblivion 'Nowhere' {
      description '
        Not a backlog, not a parking lot, not a someday list. There is one
        arrow into this element and there is no arrow out, and that is the
        complete behaviour of it.

        Nothing here is recoverable, because nothing here was ever written.
      '
    }
  }

  // =======================================================================
  // Relationships
  //
  // The two legs of the walk are one relation, not two: it is the same four
  // metres in both directions, and the sequence in `taskProposal` is where
  // the order matters.
  // =======================================================================

  office.t25 -> office.deskA 'Works at, and returns to'
  office.t37 -> office.deskB 'Works at, and does not leave'

  office.t25 -> office.deskB 'Crosses the room to, and back from — four metres, no calendar entry'

  office.t25 -> office.t37 'Proposes the task, out loud, once' #verbal
  office.t37 -> office.t25 'Declines it, on current workload rather than on merit' #verbal

  office.t25 -> office.task 'Holds it, in working memory' #unwritten
  office.t37 -> office.task 'Holds it too, and for about as long' #unwritten

  office.task -> office.nowhere 'Was never written anywhere, so this is where it is now' #unwritten
}
